# Mosquitto ACL -- copy to `acl` (gitignored) and adjust.
#
#   cp acl.example acl && docker restart mosquitto
#
# THIS FILE IS DEFAULT-DENY. A missing rule is not an error -- the broker
# silently declines to deliver. That failure mode has bitten this lab once
# already: `esp32-field` had write rules but no `topic read cmd/#`, so every
# breaker command published cleanly, returned success, and was never
# delivered. Nothing logged on either end. See docs/adr/0003-command-topic-scheme.md
#
# Principle: the ACL mirrors only what is live. Expanding it preemptively
# widens blast radius if a field credential leaks. Add rules as roles ship.

# ---- field devices (all six boards connect as this identity) ----
user esp32-field
# telemetry up: grid/<short>/<tag> and grid/<short>/status
topic write grid/#
# commands down: firmware subscribes cmd/<short>/# and cmd/all/#
# REQUIRED -- without this, commands silently never arrive.
topic read cmd/#

# ---- historian / monitoring / twin / fleet manager (read path) ----
user monitor-reader
topic read #

# ---- supervisory control (fleet manager command path, Ignition) ----
user scada-server
topic readwrite #

# ---- Topic roots reserved for roles that are not live yet. ----
# Intentionally NOT granted. Uncomment per role as its physics ships and is
# validated on hardware -- not before.
# topic write dc/substation/#
# topic write water/#
# topic write bms/#
# topic write dc/power/#
# topic write dc/cooling/#
# topic write dc/env/#
# topic write pipeline/#
